  "job": "Shoots from far back and leaves lines of morning light her team can run along.",
  "difficulty": 1,
  "lore": "Lisvel believes that light is a road. She stands at the back of the fight with an ash longbow as long as she is tall and draws a line of morning from her feet to the far side of the dial, and then she lets her friends run along it. Aubade archers are taught to hit what they aim at. Lisvel was taught to give the wind somewhere to go. She hums when she shoots, always the first four notes of the dawn song, and always stops before the fifth, in case someone behind her wants to finish it.",
